      "text": "**I’d skip a strenuous outdoor workout in Jurong right now.** It’s about **32°C**, and Singapore’s NEA forecast a **24-hour PSI of 150 for today, October 17**—at the unhealthy threshold, when healthy people should reduce prolonged or strenuous outdoor exertion. Showers are also possible. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/))\n\nA short, easy walk may be more reasonable if you feel well, but hydrate, keep it brief, and stop if you feel unwell. Check NEA’s **West-region 1-hour PM2.5** and local lightning/rain alerts before heading out; the live readings weren’t available in the page data I could verify. If you have heart or lung disease, or are pregnant, elderly, or a child, it’s safer to exercise indoors today. ([haze.gov.sg](https://www.haze.gov.sg/?trk=public_profile__reactions-text&utm_source=openai))",
